<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  SAND_SWIMMERS_MOD_1 — biome wiring: puts the sand-swimmer fish family
  (RimStarWars: SWBestiary — RSW_DuneCrawler / RSW_SandStalker / RSW_GlassPearl /
  RSW_RareSandCatches) into `ZBiome_Badlands` (the Cracked Lands, More Vanilla
  Biomes) as its `fishTypes`, replacing the vanilla Fish_Guppy/Fish_Tilapia/
  RareFishingCatches_Hot that ship on that def today.

  TARGETED, VERIFIED, NOT GUESSED: `ZBiome_Badlands` is not in the offline def dump
  or rimsage's vanilla-source index (it's a third-party BiomeDef, sarg/zylle content),
  so its live XML was read directly off disk from the active workshop copy —
  `.../steamapps/workshop/content/294100/1931453053/1.6/Defs/BiomeDefs/ZBiome_Badlands.xml`
  (packageId `zylle.MoreVanillaBiomes`, confirmed active in the live ModsConfig.xml) —
  to confirm the exact existing `<fishTypes>` shape before writing xpaths against it,
  rather than assuming vanilla's default shape applies. It already carries:
    maxFishPopulation 360; freshwater_Common Fish_Guppy(1); freshwater_Uncommon
    Fish_Tilapia(1); saltwater_Common Fish_Bluefish(1); saltwater_Uncommon
    Fish_Tuna(1); rareCatchesSetMaker RareFishingCatches_Hot.
  Only the freshwater buckets, the rare-catch pool, and the population cap are
  touched below; saltwater is left alone (ZBiome_Badlands has no salt water to
  speak of, and this item is about sand, not the ocean).

  SITING DECISION (open, surfaced rather than silently made): the item's own siting
  suggestion is "dune sea / deep desert / Cracked Lands flats" (an OR list). This
  patch targets Cracked Lands ONLY. Reason: `ExtremeDesert` — the BiomeDef backing
  BOTH the dune sea (θ0-40) and deep desert (θ50-69, Glare/Kiln) per dune_sea.md §2
  and deep_desert.md §0 — is a single shared def with no per-region hook, and
  dune_sea.md §6 hard-bans medium-sized fauna in that biome outright ("No medium-
  sized fauna. Body sizes are giant or grain-scale, nothing between" — a FROZEN
  ruling, BIOME_FREEZE_FABLE_REVIEW_1). RSW_SandStalker is deliberately mid-scale
  (bodySize 1.1, fits deep desert, which carries no such ban) — wiring ExtremeDesert
  too would silently make this family available in dune-sea tiles as well, where it
  would violate that ban the moment a world-tile placement pass drops a Deep Sand
  pool at θ<40. Cracked Lands carries no equivalent ban, so it is the only one of
  the three suggested sites this patch touches. Extending to ExtremeDesert/Desert
  (deep desert siting) is a real follow-up, gated on that conflict being resolved —
  not resolved here, and not silently dropped either.

  ANTI-EXPONENTIAL: maxFishPopulation dropped 360 -> 90 (a first-pass number, not
  measured/tuned against play — the owner's verify pass should retune it). Fish
  Nutrition/MarketValue are held at vanilla tier on the RSW side; this is the only
  yield lever touched here, and it is a straight cut, not a multiplier.
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>More Vanilla Biomes</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <success>Always</success>
      <operations>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace" MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">
          <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ZBiome_Badlands"]/fishTypes/freshwater_Common</xpath>
          <value>
            <freshwater_Common>
              <RSW_DuneCrawler MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">1</RSW_DuneCrawler>
            </freshwater_Common>
          </value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace" MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">
          <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ZBiome_Badlands"]/fishTypes/freshwater_Uncommon</xpath>
          <value>
            <!-- FISH_TYPES_PATCH_BUILD_1 (2026-09-10): the merged Cracked Lands ruling
                 (_fish_assignment_proposal.md §2/§5.1, owner-ratified) fills what was
                 deliberately left empty here — the canyon slot-water's own predator
                 pair, donors from Biomes! Caverns (BMT_, packageId
                 biomesteam.biomescaverns; already a live donor on this def's sibling
                 RUT_Greentide wildAnimals, e.g. BMT_Diggerpede). Common catch
                 everywhere in the biome stays RSW_DuneCrawler (above); this bucket now
                 pulls the deeper canyon line. The census's VCEF_Spiderfish/
                 VCEF_ShadowFry secondaries are dropped per the ruling — three species
                 is enough for one biome. -->
            <freshwater_Uncommon>
              <BMT_Rocktooth MayRequire="biomesteam.biomescaverns">1</BMT_Rocktooth>
              <BMT_Boneblade MayRequire="biomesteam.biomescaverns">1</BMT_Boneblade>
            </freshwater_Uncommon>
          </value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace" MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">
          <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ZBiome_Badlands"]/fishTypes/rareCatchesSetMaker</xpath>
          <value>
            <rareCatchesSetMaker MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">RSW_RareSandCatches</rareCatchesSetMaker>
          </value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ZBiome_Badlands"]/maxFishPopulation</xpath>
          <value>
            <maxFishPopulation>90</maxFishPopulation>
          </value>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
